.TH LCOVMERGE 1 "October 2026" "lcovmerge 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lcovmerge \- bounded-memory LCOV tracefile merger
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lcovmerge
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIa.info\fR \fIb.info\fR ... \fB-o\fR \fIout.info\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lcovmerge
merges LCOV tracefiles with a bounded record arena and temporary sorted runs. Output source files and coverage rows are sorted deterministically. Summary rows are recalculated from merged coverpoints.
.PP
The shell expands wildcard arguments before execution. Use \fB@listfile\fR to read additional input paths, one per line. A single \fB-\fR input reads standard input; output \fB-\fR writes standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI -o " FILE" ", " --output " FILE"
Write the result to FILE. The destination is replaced only after a successful file merge. Use \fB-\fR for standard output.
.TP
.BI --mem-limit " SIZE"
Set the record-arena limit. SIZE is an integer with optional K, M, or G binary suffix. The default is 64M; the minimum is 8M per job.
.TP
.BI --tmpdir " DIR"
Place sorted run files under DIR. The default is the system temporary directory. Run files are removed on completion, input errors, I/O errors, SIGINT, and SIGTERM.
.TP
.BI -j " N" ", " --jobs " N"
Generate sorted runs from up to N input files concurrently. The default is the lesser of four and the detected processor count. N is limited to 32 and constrained by the memory limit.
.TP
.BI --prefix-strip " PREFIX"
Remove PREFIX from matching SF paths.
.TP
.BI --rebase " OLD=NEW"
Replace a matching SF path prefix. May be repeated. Directory separators are preserved for drive-style paths.
.TP
.BI --include " GLOB"
Keep SF paths matching GLOB. May be repeated; when present, a path must match at least one include.
.TP
.BI --exclude " GLOB"
Drop SF paths matching GLOB. Exclusions take precedence over includes. Matching supports \fB*\fR, \fB?\fR, and bracket ranges.
.TP
.BI --branch-coverage " on|off"
Keep BRDA records (default) or omit them.
.TP
.B --no-function-data
Omit FN, FNDA, FNL, and FNA records.
.TP
.B --strict-checksum
Return input/format error status 2 when checksums for the same source line differ. The default warns and selects the lexicographically smallest non-empty checksum.
.TP
.B --warn-unknown
Print a diagnostic for every preserved unknown record.
.TP
.B -q
Suppress verbose progress output.
.TP
.B -v
Print parsed byte/record totals, selected worker count, and merged summary totals to standard error.
.TP
.B --stats
Print merged LF/LH/FNF/FNH/BRF/BRH totals to standard error.
.TP
.B --version
Print the version and build's git commit identifier.
.TP
.B --help
Print usage.
.SH INPUT RECORDS
Recognized rows include TN, SF/KF, legacy FN/FNDA, LCOV 2.x FNL/FNA, DA with optional checksum, BRDA, MCDC, and summary rows. Summary rows in inputs are ignored and generated from the merged coverpoints. Unknown colon-delimited rows inside a source section are preserved in sorted order; exact duplicate unknown rows are preserved too.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Merge completed.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid or incomplete command-line options.
.TP
.B 2
Input or tracefile format error, including strict checksum disagreement.
.TP
.B 3
Input/output or temporary-file I/O failure, allocation failure, or interruption.
.SH SEE ALSO
lcov(1), geninfo(1), genhtml(1)
